    "lawCode": "Add §458-c, RPT L",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Tax Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S1681\n\nSPONSOR: SKOUFIS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the real property tax law, in relation to establishing a\ntax exemption for improvements to the property of severely injured\nmembers of the armed forces of the United States\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo established a real property tax exemption, by local option, to\nseverely injured members of the armed forces of the United State due to\na service-connected disability who altered, installed or improved their\nprimary residence of architectural barriers and are found fit to contin-\nue military service by the physical evaluation board of such service\nmembers branch of service.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Amends real property tax law by adding a new section..\n\nSection 2: Effective date.\n\n \nEXISTING:\n\nThe property tax exemption law provided under current law only applies\nto seriously disabled veterans and not seriously disabled members of the\narmed forces still in service.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nCurrently, only veterans, not active members of the armed forces, are\neligible for a real property tax exemption. Therefore, there are seri-\nously disabled members of our armed forces who are being excluded from\nreceiving a benefit they rightfully deserve due to their decision to\ncontinue serving our country. This legislation would end this discrepan-\ncy by merely extending this property tax benefit to current members of\nthe armed forces who, despite being seriously disabled, remain in active\nservice.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nAssembly:\n2015: A.3574 (Skoufis) Referred to Veterans' Affairs Committee\n2016:  A.3574-A (Skoufis) Reported to Ways and Means Committee\n2017: A.8729 (Skoufis) Referred to Veterans' Affairs Committee\n06/20/18 - Passed Assembly\n\nSenate:\n01/03/18 - Referred to Veterans, Homeland Security and Military Affairs\n06/01/18 -Amend (t) and recommit to Veterans, Homeland Security and\nMilitary Affairs\n06/01/18 - Print Number 7001A\n06/20/18 - Delivered to Senate\n06/20/18 - Referred to Rules\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to state\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis shall take effect on the second day of January on which it shall\nhave become a law and shall apply to assessment rolls prepared on the\nbasis of taxable status date occurring on or after such date.\n",
